#!bovnar 1.1
# versioned.bvnr — demonstrates the spec 1.1 version directive
#
# The first line above is a VERSION DIRECTIVE, not an ordinary comment:
#
#   #!bovnar <major>.<minor>
#
#   • It must be the very first line (an optional UTF-8 BOM and leading
#     whitespace may precede it).
#   • It declares the bovnar spec version this document targets.
#   • Lexically it is still a comment, so a spec-1.0 reader skips it and parses
#     the rest of the document unchanged — declaring a version never breaks an
#     older parser.
#   • A 1.1+ reader records it (bvnr_reader_get_declared_version /
#     bovnar validate reports it / Python Reader.declared_version) and, in
#     strict mode, refuses a version it does not support.
#
# A #!bovnar line anywhere other than the first line is an ordinary comment.

.title   = "sensor frame";
.spec    = "bovnar 1.1";
.reading = <float:64,m/s> 9.81;
.count   = <uint:32> 1024;
